# R41 T-FMT-A §1 — the FFI-marshalling cell, and the reason the dropped
# `extern "C"` tag was a SEMANTIC defect rather than a cosmetic one.
#
# AXIS CELL: `extern "C"` + a `String` PARAMETER. `FunctionDef.extern_abi ==
# Some("C")` selects `AbiKind::CStr` at lowering, so the argument marshals via
# `gorget_str_to_cstr(...)`. Drop the tag and the SAME call passes the 32-byte
# `Str` struct BY VALUE into a `const char*` — silent UB, and this was live
# across the `extern "C"` declarations in `lib/std/`.
#
# The instrument is `gg build --emit-c-lir`: it is the only one that SEES the
# marshalling. `gg check` and `gg build` both stay green across the drop, which
# is exactly why this shipped unnoticed. Wired by
# `fmt_preserves_extern_abi_marshalling`, which diffs the emitted call between
# the original source and the `gg fmt` output.

extern "C" int gg_puts_probe(String s) = "puts"

void main():
    String msg = "hi"
    print(gg_puts_probe(msg))
